<item>
            <title>[PARQUET-1637] Builds are failing because default jdk changed to openjdk11 on Travis</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/PARQUET-1637</link>
                <project id="12315521" key="PARQUET">Parquet</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;The default distribution on Travis recently changed from Trusy to Xenial. It appears that the default JDK also changed from JDK8 to JDK11, despite the doc &lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.travis-ci.com/user/reference/xenial/#jvm-clojure-groovy-java-scala-support&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;says&lt;/a&gt; the default is openjdk8, it appears that it isn&apos;t correct (see related &lt;a href=&quot;https://travis-ci.community/t/default-jdk-on-xenial-openjdk8-or-openjdk11/4542&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;discussion&lt;/a&gt;)&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Since Parquet still doesn&apos;t support Java 11 (&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/PARQUET-1551&quot; title=&quot;Support Java 11 - top-level JIRA&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;PARQUET-1551&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;PARQUET-1551&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt;), we should explicitly tell in Travis config which JDK to use, at lease as long as &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/PARQUET-1551&quot; title=&quot;Support Java 11 - top-level JIRA&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;PARQUET-1551&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;PARQUET-1551&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; is still open.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
